# Product

Build a free, ad-free, mobile-first PWA. Working name: Delhi Metro Simple. It is an independent app, with no official DMRC affiliation.

The home task is: choose origin, choose destination, show one readable route. Answer which train, where to change, and the fare when the payload includes one.

Primary destinations are Plan, Map, and Help. Navigation is a compact top bar with an icon and a text label, so it does not cover the page. Wide screens use two panes: controls on the left, the route or the line on the right.

Out of v1: accounts, payments, ticket sales, ads, analytics, chatbots, social feeds, and mandatory install, onboarding, or location permission.

Location is requested only after “Use my location.” Saved trips stay on the device. Share links use station codes, not precise location.

Follow `docs/DMRC_API.md` for upstream calls. Follow `docs/DECISIONS.md` for defaults already made.

Files that stay on this machine and out of git are listed in the local-files rule. Do not delete them, and do not add them to a commit.

Ship through a branch and a pull request. Follow the deployment rule. Do not push straight to `main`.

Commits use `type(scope): description`. `type` is `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`, `refactor`, or `chore`. `scope` is the area that changed, such as `plan`, `map`, `city`, `offline`, `deploy`, `data`, or `docs`. The description is the change itself, in lowercase, with no period. One commit is one change. Do not use a label that does not name the work.
